  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Slot</strong> none; <strong>Price</strong> 5,000 gp (lesser), 10,000 gp (normal), 20,000 gp (greater)<br>\n<strong>Weight</strong> 5 lbs.; <strong>Feat Cost</strong> 1 sp</p>\n<p>An aquatic talent functions normally underwater and requires no magic skill check to cast, even if it has the fire descriptor. In addition, the talent can be cast from the surface into water and still be effective.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nCraft Apparatus, Aquatic Spell; <strong>Cost</strong> 2,500 gp (lesser), 5,000 gp (normal), 10,000 gp (greater)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses-metamagic#toc4\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": "<p>Selected profile: lesser tier; held slender rod. Use as part of casting a qualifying sphere effect while holding this apparatus in at least one hand. Spend one of its three daily uses; only one metamagic apparatus may apply per casting. The apparatus does not require knowing its feat or paying that feat’s extra spell points/casting time. Normal sphere-effect costs and other known metamagic costs still apply. The chosen sphere effect must be caster level 7 or lower.</p><p>Only the source underwater and surface-to-water casting permissions are granted. Do not change movement, breathing, descriptors or all magic-skill checks.</p><p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses-metamagic\">Shared metamagic apparatus rules</a>. The Feat Cost in the source applies to taking the feat instead of using the physical item.</p>",
      "unidentified": ""
    },
